  "step_3": "The decision reason emphasizes that differences in outcomes are negligible and that the preference is based solely on the higher probability of a favorable outcome. In this case, both lotteries have a 100% probability of a favorable outcome (at least 2400 Euros), so the reason would be indifferent. However, the individual does not consider or reference the probability of favorable outcomes at all. Instead, the individual evaluates the potential gain (100 Euros) and the risk of receiving nothing (1% chance), which reflects a different decision rationale — one based on risk and expected utility, not on the probability of favorable outcomes. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason. The information considered by the individual (potential gain, risk of zero) is inconsistent with the focus of the decision reason (probability of favorable outcomes). The justification also does not follow the rule of the reason (prefer higher probability of favorable outcome). Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
